<title>INDIA: India L&amp;T first half 96/97 net up 19 pct.</title>
<headline>India L&amp;T first half 96/97 net up 19 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 30, 1996</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		2,010.00  vs   1,690.00</p>
<p>    Sales		    23,620.00  vs  17,850.00</p>
<p>    Expenditure	    20,152.00  vs  15,476.00</p>
<p>    Interest		    628.30  vs     258.20</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    3,119.90  vs   2,411.20</p>
<p>    Depreciation		814.70  vs     609.60</p>
<p>    Taxation		    300.00  vs     110.00</p>
<p>    Shr (EPS in rupees)	16.14  vs	14.78</p>
<p>Note:Larsen &amp; Toubro, India's leading engineering and construction firm, said its new cement unit in Gujarat and glass works in Maharashtra started commercial production during the first half. It alloted secured redeemable non-convertible debentures for 5.0 billion rupees effective November 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
